  "title": "Gertrude Bell",
  "summary": "Gertrude Bell, born in County Durham in 1868, became a British administrator in Mesopotamia. She attended the 1921 Cairo Conference and, with T.E. Lawrence, backed Feisal as king of Iraq. As Honorary Director of Antiquities she helped found the Iraq Museum in Baghdad, where she died in July 1926.",
